When travelling abroad, it is important to be aware of your surroundings and take precautions to avoid security cameras. Be mindful of any surveillance cameras in public places such as stores, streets, and transportation hubs. If possible, try to use alternative routes that do not involve passing by these areas. If you must pass by a camera, make sure to be respectful and not engage in any suspicious activities. Additionally, be mindful of what you post on social media as some countries have laws that require individuals to obtain permission before taking photos or videos in public spaces. Finally, always remember to respect the privacy of others and do not take pictures or videos without their consent. 
